# name  = user-edit.check_pending_excursions
# descr = run pending out-of-loop terminal excursions after zenka.loop returns

## the shared resume point for "leave the event loop, run something blocking
## on the terminal, come back" excursions triggered MID-SESSION -- today the
## only one is the key-actions tab's key-create [ <user-edit.pending.
## key_create>, set by plugin.user-edit.key-actions.handler.key right before
## its Event::unloop() ], shaped exactly after the bootstrap create-offer's
## own <user-edit.pending.create> contract.
##
## called after BOTH <[base.zenka.loop]> call sites that a mid-session unloop
## can resume into -- user-edit.console.start's own AND user-edit.
## offer_create's nested one [ active instead whenever this session went
## through the create-admin bootstrap first ].  handling only one site would
## silently end the session in the other case : the loop returns, nothing
## checks the pending flag, and the caller falls through to its return.
##
## a WHILE, not an if : the action can fire more than once in one session.
## each iteration re-enters <[base.zenka.loop]> itself, and that call returns
## again on the NEXT excursion's unloop.  the real session quit never resumes
## here at all -- user-edit.form.quit ends in <[base.exit]>, so the process
## exits from inside the loop rather than unwinding back to this frame.
##
## the STDIN io-watcher is deliberately LEFT REGISTERED throughout : Event is
## not pumping between unloop and the re-entry below, perl is single-threaded,
## and the blocking reads inside the excursion are the only thing touching fd
## 0 meanwhile.  term_restore / term_init toggle O_NONBLOCK and the termios
## mode, which is what actually governs blocking and raw-vs-canonical -- the
## same implicit assumption offer_create's blocking base.term.ask already
## relies on, exercised here with a watcher that was already active.

while (<user-edit.pending.key_create>) {

    <user-edit.pending.key_create> = FALSE;

    <[user-edit.term_restore]>;

    ## prompts, pre-validates and creates -- sets <user-edit.key_actions.
    ## last_result> either way [ see that module's own header for the
    ## keys.console.create base.exit risk this ordering exists for ]
    <[user-edit.excursion.key_create]>;

    <[user-edit.term_init]>;

    ## repaint once the loop pumps again, so the tab shows the outcome ##
    <user-edit.form.dirty>++;

    ## re-enter ; returns again on the next excursion's unloop [ the real
    ## end-of-session quit exits the process from inside the loop instead ]
    <[base.zenka.loop]>;
}

return TRUE;

